{
"body": "Start Time: October 20, 2025 at 07:10 UTC\nEnd Time: October 20, 2025 at 10:53 PM UTC\n\nSummary:\nSome customers may have experienced slow sync performance and intermittent errors during the global AWS outage on October 20, 2025.\n\nCause:\nThe issue was caused by an incident in the AWS us-east-1 region, impacting several dependent services and resulting in temporary sync delays and connection timeouts.\n\nResolution:\nAfter AWS restored stability across their services, Hevo systems automatically recovered, and all sync operations have returned to normal.\n\nNext Steps:\nWe continue to monitor platform performance closely and are taking measures to further strengthen resilience against third-party service disruptions.",
